{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And from Mattanah.</b> They came to <b>Nahaliel</b> — meaning a wadi and a valley. As it is stated in the portion of Masei: ״ויסעו [מעיי] מהרי העברים ויחנו בערבות מואב״ — this is the last encampment." "<b>And from Nahaliel.</b> They spread out to <b>Bamoth</b> — this is what is called בית הישימות in the portion of Masei, meaning desolation. As our Sages taught: they would call it בית גליא; they call it בית כריא — עין כל עין קוץ."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {0 "The bracketed [מעיי] appears in the source; its reading is uncertain.", 1 "The phrase עין כל עין קוץ is obscure; translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:19:03.737783198Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}